{c: Chords from the writer's own lead sheet (MusicXML in the source above)}

{start_of_verse: Intro}
Glory to Your [Gmaj7]Name!
[Bm7]Glory to Your [Gmaj7]Name!
[Bm7]Glory to Your [Em7]Name!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Risen and [Dmaj7]conquering [D]King.
[D]Humbly we [Bsus2]praise.
[D]Master of [Dmaj7]every[D]thing.
[D]Now and al[Bsus2]ways.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
You [Gsus2]traded splendor [A]You deserve,
[Bm7]And [Gsus2]bought us at great [A]price.
[D]You [Gsus2]paid a debt that [A]was not Yours
[Bm7]And [Gsus2]brought us back to [A]life.
[Bm7]Glory to Your [Gsus2]Name!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gsus2]Fulfilling what the [A]prophets said,
[Bm7]You [Gsus2]gave all You could [A]give,
[D]Then, [Gsus2]rising, crushed the [A]serpent's head
[Bm7]That [Gsus2]stillborn souls might [A]live!
[Bm7]Glory to Your [Gmaj7]Name!
[Bm7]Glory to Your [Gmaj7]Name!
[Bm7]Glory to Your [Em7]Name!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge}
[D5]Jesus, Saviour,
[Bm7]Mighty Conqueror —
[Asus4]Now [A]and for[G]ever You will [D]reign.
{end_of_bridge}
